## Follow-up Questions

- How would you scale to 10k tenants with isolated streams?
- How would you validate behavior if the WebSocket layer fails and you must fall back to long-polling?

## Why This Is Asked
This question probes practical idempotency testing in a distributed system, covering state stores, event emission, concurrency, and failure modes.

## Key Concepts
- Idempotent operations and deduplication windows
- Durable storage guarantees and TTL management
- Concurrency control and race conditions
- Failure modes and graceful degradation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-handler: on POST /orders with idempotencyKey
if (!store.has(key)) {
  const order = createOrder(payload);
  publishKafka(order);
  store.set(key, order.id, ttl);
  return { status: 200, body: { orderId: order.id } };
} else {
  return { status: 200, body: { orderId: store.get(key) } };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test TTL-based key reuse vs. hard deduplication windows?
- How would you monitor and alert on rising duplicate requests or stuck idempotency keys?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to validate real-time streaming APIs under multi-tenant constraints, including data isolation, ordering guarantees, and resilience to failures. It also covers dynamic feature flags via an admin API, which is common in production environments.

## Key Concepts

- WebSocket streaming and per-tenant scoping
- Message ordering and deduplication in a high-throughput channel
- Reconnection/backoff logic and backpressure handling
- Dynamic feature flags via admin API and their impact on clients
- Fault injection: broker outages, network partitions, and fallback behavior

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal WebSocket test scaffold (conceptual)
const WebSocket = require('ws');
const ws = new WebSocket(`wss://api.example.com/ws/tenantA/orders`);
let lastTs = 0;
ws.on('message', (data) => {
  const msg = JSON.parse(data);
  // verify monotonic timestamp and non-duplication
  if (msg.ts <= lastTs) throw new Error('Out-of-order or duplicate message');
  lastTs = msg.ts;
});
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you simulate clock skew or message replays to test idempotency and replay protection?
- How would you scale these tests to verify behavior across dozens of tenants concurrently while keeping test isolation?
